    {
      "name": "urgency_and_blocker_status",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.78,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a blocker/urgency axis distinct from the original 'priority' column, offering a genuine new dimension to model resolution time against. Values are soundly inferred from text (outage, revenue risk, enhancement-only, user friction). Partially overlaps conceptually with priority but is derived from description content, not redundant."
    },
    {
      "name": "issue_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.68,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Provides a finer taxonomy (bug vs feature vs outage vs billing error) that partially overlaps with issue_theme but adds a bug/request/error distinction useful for analysis. Grounded well, though CS-0002 labeled 'bug_functionality' when it is arguably an auth/session issue, a slight categorisation mismatch. Some redundancy with issue_theme lowers usefulness modestly."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.89,
  "rationale": "All three columns supply grounded, query-relevant axes (theme, urgency/blocker, type) for analyzing resolution time. issue_theme is the strongest; issue_type overlaps somewhat with issue_theme but still adds a bug/request/error lens. Values across the row samples are sound readings of the source text with only minor debatable categorisations and no invented facts."
}

